export const NOTES = "Germany (Kriegsmarine) - 5 ship classes. No flags, ensigns or markings are described; data is hull geometry and gameplay stats only. Graf Zeppelin was launched 8 Dec 1938 but never completed or commissioned (about 85% finished, work stopped 1940 and 1943, scuttled 1945); the sheet gives the design as built/planned, and 'commissioned' is null for that reason. Class rosters: Konigsberg class had only 3 ships, Bismarck class 2, Graf Zeppelin class 2 (one launched), Hipper class 3 completed plus 2 unfinished, so the 4-8 ship guideline cannot be met for several classes. Type 1936A (Mob) hero ship is Z39 (twin 15 cm turret forward plus three single 15 cm guns aft); the early Type 1936A (Z23-Z30) had only single mounts forward. Gun boreCalibers uses the German nominal L/xx designation (e.g. 38 cm L/52 is 51.7 calibers overall, 48.4 bore). Longitudinal fractions for guns, funnels, masts and AA mounts are estimated from profile knowledge and are not in the cited text; Bismarck turret fractions were derived from published frame numbers (Anton 192.55, Bruno 174.35, Caesar 64.35, Dora 46.15 on a roughly 1.1 m frame spacing). Prinz Eugen dimensions are those with the clipper bow added after launch (212.5 m).";
